 "report": "_claude/builds/reports/agent-cap.md",
 "open": [
  "The heavy lock is opt-in per command (`agent-slots.mjs heavy -- …`): the brief tells every headless session to use it, but nothing forces a session that ignores it. A PreToolUse hook that wraps matching Bash commands would make it hard.",
  "Orchestrator / build-manager / systems-check / push-banner launches go through `claude-headless.sh` and so are capped; their nohup fallback (no helper script on the host) is not.",
  "The activity banner only shows while something is active, so the slots chip shows with it, not on its own.",
  "Android: nothing (web/TS/Python only; no cross-port contract changed)."
 ]
